# Workflow: Test Hierarchy

Purpose:
   Define three test execution levels (SUBTASK, MODULE, SYSTEM) that map
   to the Q→T→ST hierarchy and provide increasing scope validation.
   Each level has specific triggers, scopes, types, runners, and owners.

Owns: workflow/test-hierarchy.sdd

TestLevels:

   SUBTASK level:
     - Triggered: after each ST implementation
     - Scope: single subtask's changed files
     - Types: Unit (T0), Feature/Integration (T1/T3), API/Contract (T2)
     - Runner: local Docker (builder service)
     - Owner: implementer agent

   MODULE level:
     - Triggered: when all STs for a module are DONE
     - Scope: entire module (all STs combined)
     - Types: Integration, Component (T3), E2E (T4) within module
     - Regression: previous module functionality
     - Runner: local Docker
     - Owner: QA agent + implementer

   SYSTEM level:
     - Triggered: when all modules for a decision are DONE
     - Scope: cross-module business flows
     - Types: E2E (T4), Performance (T5), Security (T6), Acceptance (T7)
     - Runner: local Docker (full stack)
     - Owner: QA + Business

TestExecution:
   SUBTASK test:
     docker compose run --rm <builder> npm test -- --testPathPattern="<subtask_scope>"

   MODULE test:
     docker compose run --rm test-runner ./run-module-tests.sh <module_name>

   SYSTEM test:
     docker compose run --rm test-runner ./run-system-tests.sh <decision_id>

Rules:
   [TH1] Test levels MUST be executed in order: SUBTASK → MODULE → SYSTEM
   [TH2] Each level MUST pass before advancing to the next level
   [TH3] Test scope MUST match the declared level (no scope creep)
   [TH4] All test execution MUST run inside Docker ([R102], [W19])
   [TH5] Test results MUST be recorded in done_proof for aggregation

